{
  "summary": "Replaces the `-privatebroadcast` implementation with isolated, stateless background jobs managed under a new `src/privbcast` module. Submitted transactions bypass the local mempool and connection manager, running on dedicated threads that resolve DNS seeds via Tor and announce transactions over BIP324 on a fixed schedule using isolated proxy credentials for every connection. Completely removes legacy `ConnectionType::PRIVATE_BROADCAST` connections, retry tasks, and special-case handling from `CConnman` and `PeerManager`.",
  "problem": "The existing private broadcast mechanism was intertwined with the node's main connection manager and peer logic, introducing special cases across addrman, peer discouragement, and connection tracking. This coupling risked deanonymization and IP linkage through shared node state while complicating maintainability of core P2P networking.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'test profile focusing on protecting aginst IP address linkage and not crashing the node on adversarial inputs (which is a leak in itself)'",
    "Commit 03435a45ef: 'The plan is drawn when the job is made, before any socket exists... slots share only the loop, so a stalled stream holds up no other slot'",
    "PR description: 'Split out of #36608, the overall private broadcast rework to support ease of review for like-for-like feature.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36608"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Very large diff (+6341/-3046 across 78 files) that adds a standalone byte-driven SOCKS5 and BIP324 network engine in src/privbcast/, introduces a formal invariant specification in doc/design/private-broadcast.md, and removes hundreds of lines of legacy private broadcast plumbing from net.cpp and net_processing.cpp.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased onto newer master commits; the core architecture, specification, and module structure remain identical.",
  "card": "Replaces the existing private broadcast subsystem with isolated, stateless background jobs managed under a new src/privbcast module. When -privatebroadcast is enabled, transactions bypass the local mempool and connection manager, executing on dedicated threads that discover peers via DNS seeds and announce over BIP324 strictly through Tor using isolated proxy credentials and a fixed schedule. This eliminates IP linkage and node-state correlation vectors while removing invasive private-broadcast special-case logic from CConnman and PeerManager. It unblocks follow-up package relay support for private broadcast in #36608.",
